1
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:03,719
Chapter 103.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:07,550
measurement of the whale's skeleton.

3
00:00:07,551 --> 00:00:12,359
In the first place, I wish to lay before you a particular plain statement

4
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:16,599
touching the living bulk of this Leviathan whose skeleton we are briefly

5
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,638
to exhibit, such a statement may prove useful here.

6
00:00:21,639 --> 00:00:26,678
According to a careful calculation I have made and which I partly base upon

7
00:00:26,679 --> 00:00:32,599
Captain Scoresby's estimate of 70 tons for the largest size Greenland whale of

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:38,830
60 ft in length. According to my careful calculation I say a sperm whale of the

9
00:00:38,831 --> 00:00:44,918
largest magnitude between 85 and 90 ft in length and something less than 40 ft

10
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:50,511
in its fullest circumference. Such a whale will weigh at least 90 tons. so

11
00:00:50,512 --> 00:00:55,799
that reckoning 13 men to a ton, he would considerably outweigh the combined

12
00:00:55,800 --> 00:01:01,398
population of a whole village of 1,100 inhabitants.

13
00:01:01,399 --> 00:01:05,638
Think you not then that brains like yolked cattle should be put to this

14
00:01:05,639 --> 00:01:11,799
Leviathan to make him at all budge to any landsman's imagination?

15
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:17,159
Having already in various ways put before you his skull, spout hole, jaw,

16
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:23,079
teeth, tail, forehead, fins, and diverse other parts, I shall now simply point

17
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:28,278
out what is most interesting in the general bulk of his unobstructed bones.

18
00:01:28,279 --> 00:01:33,159
But as the colossal skull embraces so very large a proportion of the entire

19
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:38,190
extent of the skeleton, as it is by far the most complicated part, and as

20
00:01:38,191 --> 00:01:43,239
nothing is to be repeated concerning it in this chapter, you must not fail to

21
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:48,511
carry it in your mind or under your arm as we proceed. Otherwise, you will not

22
00:01:48,512 --> 00:01:53,871
gain a complete notion of the general structure we are about to view.

23
00:01:53,872 --> 00:01:59,550
In length, the sperm whale's skeleton at tran measured 72 feet, so that when

24
00:01:59,551 --> 00:02:04,999
fully invested and extended in life, he must have been 90 feet long. For in the

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,599
whale, the skeleton loses about 1/5th in length compared with the living body. Of

26
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:17,398
this 72 ft, his skull and jaw comprised some 20 ft, leaving some 50 ft of plain

27
00:02:17,399 --> 00:02:21,959
backbone. Attached to this backbone, for something less than a third of its

28
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:28,118
length, was the mighty circular basket of ribs which once enclosed his vitals.

29
00:02:28,119 --> 00:02:34,678
To me this vast ivory ribbed chest with the long unreieved spine extending far

30
00:02:34,679 --> 00:02:39,159
away from it in a straight line not a little resembled the hull of a great

31
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:45,079
ship new laid upon the stocks when only some 20 of her naked bow ribs are

32
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:51,719
inserted and the keel is otherwise for the time but a long disconnected timber.

33
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:57,478
The ribs were 10 on a side. The first to begin from the neck was nearly six feet

34
00:02:57,479 --> 00:03:02,511
long. The second, third, and fourth were each successively longer till you came

35
00:03:02,512 --> 00:03:08,190
to the climax of the fifth or one of the middle ribs, which measured 8 ft and

36
00:03:08,191 --> 00:03:12,999
some inches. From that part, the remaining ribs diminished, till the 10th

37
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:18,758
and last only spanned 5 ft and some inches. In general thickness, they all

38
00:03:18,759 --> 00:03:23,319
bore a seemly correspondence to their length. The middle ribs were the most

39
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:28,830
arched. In some of the arcs, they are used for beams whereon to lay footpath

40
00:03:28,831 --> 00:03:32,038
bridges over small streams.

41
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:36,439
In considering these ribs, I could not but be struck a new with the

42
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:41,159
circumstance so variously repeated in this book that the skeleton of the whale

43
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:47,239
is by no means the mold of his invested form. The largest of the tran ribs, one

44
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:52,118
of the middle ones, occupied that part of the fish, which in life is greatest

45
00:03:52,119 --> 00:03:57,799
in depth. Now, the greatest depth of the invested body of this particular whale

46
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:03,079
must have been at least 16 ft, whereas the corresponding rib measured but

47
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:08,511
little more than 8 ft, so that this rib only conveyed half of the true notion of

48
00:04:08,512 --> 00:04:11,398
the living magnitude of that part.

49
00:04:11,399 --> 00:04:16,599
Besides, for some way, where I now saw but a naked spine, all that had been

50
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:21,239
once wrapped round with tons of added bulk in flesh, muscle, blood, and

51
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:27,719
bowels, still more, for the ample fins, I here saw but a few disordered joints,

52
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:34,758
and in place of the weighty and majestic but boneless flukes, an utter blank.

53
00:04:34,759 --> 00:04:40,038
How vain and foolish then, thought I, for timid, untraveled man to try to

54
00:04:40,039 --> 00:04:44,918
comprehend a right this wondrous whale by merely pouring over his dead

55
00:04:44,919 --> 00:04:51,398
attenuated skeleton stretched in this peaceful wood. No, only in the heart of

56
00:04:51,399 --> 00:04:56,999
quickest perils, only when within the eddings of his angry flukes, only on the

57
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:02,439
profound unbounded sea can the fully invested whale be truly and livingly

58
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:08,599
found out. But the spine, for that the best way we can consider it is with a

59
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:12,278
crane to pile its bones high up on end.

60
00:05:12,279 --> 00:05:18,511
No speedy enterprise. But now it's done, it looks much like Pompy's pillar. There

61
00:05:18,512 --> 00:05:23,719
are 40 and odd vertebrae in all, which in the skeleton are not locked together.

62
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:29,398
They mostly lie like the great knobbed blocks on a Gothic spire, forming solid

63
00:05:29,399 --> 00:05:35,638
courses of heavy masonry. The largest, a middle one, is in width something less

64
00:05:35,639 --> 00:05:39,319
than 3 ft and in depth more than four.

65
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:44,118
The smallest, where the spine tapers away into the tail, is only 2 in in

66
00:05:44,119 --> 00:05:48,918
width and looks something like a white billiard ball. I was told that there

67
00:05:48,919 --> 00:05:53,159
were still smaller ones, but that they had been lost by some little cannibal

68
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:58,359
urchins, the priest's children, who had stolen them to play marbles with. Thus

69
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:03,478
we see how that the spine of even the hugest of living things tapers off at

70
00:06:03,479 --> 00:06:08,479
last into simple child's play.
